1. Introduction

The research paper focuses on the growing role of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in financial markets, especially in algorithmic trading. Traditional trading strategies rely heavily on human judgment and basic technical indicators, which often fail in highly volatile and complex markets.

This paper proposes an AI-driven trading framework that combines:

Machine Learning models
Technical indicators
Risk management techniques

The goal is to improve prediction accuracy, profitability, and trading efficiency.

  2. Objectives of the Study

The main objectives of the research are:

To develop an intelligent trading system using AI
To combine multiple technical indicators for better decision-making
To reduce risks using automated risk management strategies
To compare AI-based trading performance with traditional methods

3. Methodology

The research uses a structured approach to design the AI trading system.

📊 a) Data Collection
Historical stock market data is used
Includes:
Stock prices
Volume
Market trends
🤖 b) Machine Learning Models

The system applies machine learning algorithms such as:

Supervised learning models
Predictive models for price movement

These models learn patterns from past data to predict:

Future stock prices
Buy/Sell signals
📈 c) Hybrid Technical Indicators

Instead of relying on a single indicator, the paper combines multiple indicators like:

Moving Averages
RSI (Relative Strength Index)
MACD (Moving Average Convergence Divergence)

👉 This hybrid approach improves accuracy because:

One indicator alone can give false signals
Multiple indicators confirm trends more reliably
⚠️ d) Risk Management System

A major contribution of this paper is its focus on risk control. The system includes:

Stop-loss mechanisms
Position sizing
Portfolio balancing

This helps to:

Minimize losses
Protect capital during market fluctuations
